 a Converge show, George Pettit and Dallas Green later went to an Elk's Lodge to see Vincent Black Shadow perform, further illustrating the grassroots, community-driven nature of the music scene at the time. \"And then we went to some like Elk's Lodge to go see Vincent Black Shadow play one time.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Vincent Black Shadow","from_id":138732664453122,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alexisonfire - In Their Own Words Podcast","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nEPT8ZVZ0so"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Influences: Screamo, Melodic Hardcore, and Converge","body":"At the time of the band's formation (2000–2001), emo was not a mainstream genre. Their influences included melodic hardcore, early screamo (bands such as Sasha and Page 99), hardcore, and post-hardcore. Converge was a shared influence among members. \"At their formation, 'emo' was not a mainstream genre; their influences included melodic hardcore, early screamo, and Converge.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Alexisonfire","from_id":248499172879327,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alexisonfire: In Their Own Words","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FvtBph3rNF8"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Meeting at a Converge Show","body":"George Pettit and Dallas Green met Liam from Cancer Bats (who was then in Vincent Black Shadow) while waiting in line to see a Converge show, highlighting the close-knit nature of the underground music scene where many of these artists connected. \"George and I met, we met Liam from the Cancer Bats in line at a Converge show.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Cancer Bats","from_id":176819672595685,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alexisonfire - In Their Own Words Podcast","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nEPT8ZVZ0so"}]}],"charts":[{"id":202831278899767,"type":"album","name":"Petitioning the Empty Sky","list_i